# Only the staged environment is tracked: the contract, the control files, the dependency pin, the
# lock and the installed skill. Nothing a run produces is ever committed -- a committed FINDINGS.md,
# workspace or scenario would hand the next agent the previous agent's answers, which is exactly
# what the isolation exists to prevent. README.md says how to restage paper/ and data/.
FINDINGS.md
SCENARIO.md
data/
paper/
workspace/
outputs/
build/
.vqapr/
# Whatever a run writes. Run 2 and run 3 used out/, work/, prep/ and runs/; none of them were
# ignored, so the run's own answers were one `git add -A` away from being committed. An agent
# names its own directories, so keep this list current at staging time and prefer `git add -p`.
out/
work/
prep/
runs/
scratch/
.venv/
__pycache__/
.gjc/
# uv.lock is tracked: the venv must be reproducible byte-for-byte across runs.
